# S's statements are checked whether or not S runs (slice 2c-2): S has a procedure because its body has a
# statement, as a unit named Structure does (§12).  `v: nosuch` reads a free name of that body which nothing
# here binds, and nothing calls S: a body never executed keeps its free names (#construction), a caller of S
# could give nosuch (#dynamic), and nothing is missing.  m returns 7.  Entry 7.
# Until 2026-10-05 this row expected "unresolved name" at nosuch, as if a free name nobody binds were refused
# wherever it stands; that is this implementation's limit, not a rule (DORMANT-BODY-FREE-INPUT).
fn: m () int
    S:
        size_t: v 4U
        v: nosuch
    return: 7
end: m
int: r 0
r: m()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
